2026-11-07T11:51:11.5426699Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-11-07T11:51:11.5436082Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-11-07T11:51:11.5436520Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-11-07T11:51:11.5436838Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-11-07T11:51:11.5437082Z 
2026-11-07T11:51:11.5437269Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-11-07T11:51:11.5437541Z 
2026-11-07T11:51:11.5437769Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-11-07T11:51:11.5438259Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-11-07T11:51:11.5438514Z 
2026-11-07T11:51:11.5438633Z If you would like to
2026-11-07T11:51:11.5438919Z see the output, try like this:
2026-11-07T11:51:11.5439137Z 
2026-11-07T11:51:11.5439322Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-11-07T11:51:11.5439763Z   $ sh ./install-nix
2026-11-07T11:51:11.5439936Z 
